 10:
 11:/*
 12: * Z80 card address GAL (ATF22V10C-7).
 13: *
 14: * 1. Makes every Z80 I/O access look like ONE 6502 bus cycle, so the
 15: *    existing I/O cards work unchanged.
 16: *      Z80 I/O cycle:  T1  T2  TW*  T3      (IORQ low from T2 rise)
 17: *      F1 = set on the falling edge of T2 (first falling edge in the cycle)
 18: *      F2 = set on the falling edge of TW (second falling edge)
 19: *      bus /IO_EN = F2 & I/O cycle  -> opens just after TW falls, closes
 20: *               when the Z80 releases /IORQ after T3 falls. Exactly one
 21: *               clock-high (T3) is inside it, like a 6502 cycle.
 22: *      bus /IOw  = window & write  (not clock-gated: 6551/VIA R/W input)
 23: *      bus /IOr  = window & read & CLK  (read strobe)
 24: *    Interrupt acknowledge (M1 & IORQ) is excluded, so no card sees it.
 25: *    Ports = the low address byte: 6502 $7F1C -> Z80 port $1C, etc.
 26: *
 27: * 2. Self-stretch: every I/O cycle gets T3-high extended by one OSC2X
 28: *    period (T3 high = 250 ns at 4 MHz). The Z80 needs read data 30-50 ns
 29: *    before T3 falls, which a 125 ns T3 can't give slower cards (PICO9918
 30: *    worst case 86 ns after its /CSR). Cards can still ask for more with
 31: *    the bus IOREADY or /STRETCH lines (tied together on this card).
 32: *
 33: * 3. Memory map (on-card RAM and ROM):
 34: *      ROM_DIS = 0 (after reset): reads $0000-$7FFF come from ROM,
 35: *                writes there go to the RAM underneath; $8000-$FFFF RAM.
 36: *      ROM_DIS = 1: RAM everywhere ($0000-$FFFF).
 37: *      $8000-$FFFF is banked: RAM A16 = BA16 there (2 banks of 32K with
 38: *      the 128K RAM); $0000-$7FFF always uses RAM A16 = 0.
 39: *    RAM and ROM /OE come straight from Z80 /RD, RAM /WE from Z80 /WR;
 40: *    the selects below include /MREQ, so I/O and refresh cycles can't
 41: *    read or write memory.
 42: *
 43: * NOT handled (no pins left): tri-stating the bus outputs during /BUSACK.
 44: * Revisit when a DMA card exists.
 45: */
 46:
 47:/* *************** INPUT PINS *********************/
 48:PIN 1  = nCLKI ;     /* /CLK (74ACT74 FF1 /Q) - register clock        */
 49:PIN 2  = BA16 ;      /* bank bit from the interrupt GAL (U7 pin 18)   */
 50:PIN 3  = A15 ;
 51:PIN 4  = nSTRBUS ;   /* bus IOREADY + /STRETCH (tied together), low = stretch */
 52:PIN 5  = nIORQ ;     /* Z80 /IORQ                                     */
 53:PIN 6  = ROMDIS ;    /* U7 pin 22, 0 after reset                      */

LISTING FOR LOGIC DESCRIPTION FILE: Z80_ADDR.pld                     Page 2

